rows.quote_en:
An abnormal reaction to vaccination means an adverse drug reaction in which a qualified vaccine, during or after standard vaccination, causes damage to the tissues, organs or functions of the vaccinee's body, with no party concerned at fault.
The following situations are not abnormal reactions to vaccination:
(1) common reactions after vaccination caused by the inherent properties of the vaccine;
(2) damage caused to the vaccinee by vaccine quality problems;
(3) damage caused to the vaccinee by the vaccination unit's violation of vaccination work norms, immunisation schedules, guidelines for vaccine use or vaccination plans;
(4) coincidental onset of disease after vaccination where the vaccinee was in the incubation or prodromal period of a disease at the time of vaccination;
(5) acute recurrence or aggravation of a pre-existing disease after vaccination where the vaccinee had a contraindication specified in the vaccine package insert and, before vaccination, the vaccinee or the guardian did not truthfully provide the vaccinee's health status, contraindications and other information;
(6) individual or group psychogenic reactions caused by psychological factors.
